{{- /*
resolve-op-refs-json.tmpl — recursively render data as JSON while resolving
1Password references by VALUE, never by field name.

Input (dict):
  value     required; any map, slice, scalar, or null
  indent    optional; indentation of the value's containing line (default "")

Every string beginning exactly with "op://" is resolved by a direct
onepasswordRead (which CI stubs) WHEN resolveSecrets is true, and emitted verbatim
as a reference when it is false. Every other scalar and type is serialized
unchanged. Maps and slices recurse, so the rule applies uniformly to heterogeneous
provider options, nested headers, model definitions, MCP data, and auth data
without field-specific branches.

resolveSecrets is this repository's single seam between an image build and a
running pod. Both have the `container` fact true, so only `opAvailable` tells them
apart: false at build (no credential enters a layer; the reference is what lands),
true in the pod, where the entrypoint re-applies exactly these targets against
1Password Connect and the real value replaces the reference.

IT DEFAULTS TO FALSE ON PURPOSE. A consumer that forgets the argument emits an
unresolved reference, which whatever reads that file will report loudly. The other
default fails silently and in the worst direction — a credential baked into a
public image layer.

Map keys are emitted in deterministic lexical order.

Input (continued):
  resolveSecrets  optional bool; resolve op:// references (default false)

Usage (a consuming template reads the fact once and passes it down):
  {{ $facts := includeTemplate "facts.tmpl" . | fromYaml }}
  {{ includeTemplate "resolve-op-refs-json.tmpl" (dict
       "value" .agents.mcp.servers
       "indent" "  "
       "resolveSecrets" $facts.opAvailable) }}

The fact is read by the CONSUMER, once, not here: facts.tmpl globs and stats, and
this partial recurses once per node.
*/ -}}
{{- if not (kindIs "map" .) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "resolve-op-refs-json.tmpl: expected a dict, got %s" (kindOf .)) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if not (hasKey . "value") -}}
{{-   fail "resolve-op-refs-json.tmpl: missing required argument value" -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $value := .value -}}
{{-   $indent := "" -}}
{{-   if hasKey . "indent" -}}{{- $indent = .indent -}}{{- end -}}
{{-   $resolveSecrets := false -}}
{{-   if hasKey . "resolveSecrets" -}}
{{-     if not (kindIs "bool" .resolveSecrets) -}}
{{-       fail (printf "resolve-op-refs-json.tmpl: resolveSecrets must be a bool, got %s" (kindOf .resolveSecrets)) -}}
{{-     end -}}
{{-     $resolveSecrets = .resolveSecrets -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{-   $childIndent := printf "%s  " $indent -}}
{{-   if kindIs "map" $value -}}
{{-     if eq (len $value) 0 -}}
{}
{{-     else -}}
{{-       $orderedKeys := keys $value | sortAlpha -}}
{
{{-       $last := sub (len $orderedKeys) 1 -}}
{{-       range $index, $key := $orderedKeys }}
{{ $childIndent }}{{ $key | toJson }}: {{ includeTemplate "resolve-op-refs-json.tmpl" (dict "value" (index $value $key) "indent" $childIndent "resolveSecrets" $resolveSecrets) }}{{ if lt $index $last }},{{ end }}
{{-       end }}
{{ $indent }}}
{{-     end -}}
{{-   else if kindIs "slice" $value -}}
{{-     if eq (len $value) 0 -}}
[]
{{-     else -}}
[
{{-       $last := sub (len $value) 1 -}}
{{-       range $index, $item := $value }}
{{ $childIndent }}{{ includeTemplate "resolve-op-refs-json.tmpl" (dict "value" $item "indent" $childIndent "resolveSecrets" $resolveSecrets) }}{{ if lt $index $last }},{{ end }}
{{-       end }}
{{ $indent }}]
{{-     end -}}
{{-   else if and (kindIs "string" $value) (hasPrefix "op://" $value) -}}
{{-     if $resolveSecrets -}}
{{- onepasswordRead $value | toJson }}
{{-     else -}}
{{ $value | toJson }}
{{-     end -}}
{{-   else -}}
{{ $value | toJson }}
{{-   end -}}
